- Handle errors and limitations: when compilation fails, repair the test by adjusting method calls, signatures, imports, object construction, package, or by switching to other candidate methods from the scenario. When runtime errors occur, update the test if it is wrong. If the failure reveals a real defect in the application, keep the failing assertion if it matches the intended behavior. If a step is noncritical and repeatedly causes compilation errors, you may omit it from the test. Record the reason with `modify_scenario_comment` and mention the omitted step when you finalize. If a step cannot be implemented at all, still produce the most complete compilable test you can and describe the gap.

